Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, openssh-client, djvulibre-bin
Recommends: libio-socket-ip-perl
Description: Remote terminal optimized for bandwidth-constrained links
 Goblin Skiff is a fork of Mosh, optimized for bandwidth-constrained links.
 It adds zstd-22 compression, adaptive per-direction
 pacing, idle keepalive backoff, terminal graphics, and a two-pane file
 transfer menu using librsync and forward error correction.
 .
 Includes the client, server, goblin-skiffcp, dictionary compiler, manual
 pages, and shell completion.
